    "Implement pure build_payload(rom, baseline_raw, contract_raw)->dict and derive_closure(rom, roots, code_ranges, literal_ranges, opaque_entries, holes)->dict; no file IO/publication/import of upstream producers or verifiers in implementation.",
    "Pin this complete CONTRACT SHA in implementation; production build verifies exact ROM and raw baseline SHA/size before parse. Parent independent verifier binds source files and compressed baseline, replays raw upstream membership and opaque entries.",
    "Implement scan_producers(rom, targets) for full-ROM aligned Thumb B/BL/Bcond target-limited syntactic hits including final 2-byte halfword; not a global code claim. Production results must exactly match ordered raw fields of expected_producers, then verify baseline provenance before copying.",
    "Decode every actual node and derive worklist, full code/literal domains, maximal basic blocks split after calls, indirect frontiers, literal loads, preserved holes. Support only Thumb-1 encodings needed by frozen wrappers plus generic B/conditionalB/BL for hidden inputs; unknown/high-reg PC writes/SWI fail closed. No structured return inference from POP/BX. Entering code middle, literal, hole, outside ROM, or unlisted opaque target fails.",
    "BL targets in opaque_entries stop at exact entry; continue fallthrough. BX remains indirect_pc_target with register. Literal PC formula aligned(source+4)+imm8*4 and every declared literal word needs actual LDR consumer. Every supplied code byte must be reached exactly once, no instruction overlap.",
    "Root Thumb pointer occurrence scan must cover unaligned byte offsets too; bind exact denominator to public contract.",
    "All five promotion ranges must be wholly unknown in continuous immutable baseline; copy full baseline segment objects. Do not claim either two-byte hole or any adjacent bytes.",
